  "doctrine": [],
  "note": "Arabic ḏ and the Aramaic d forms illuminate Hebrew z. Related Akkadian and Geʿez words denote other predators. The atlas records Maltese díb, whereas Ġabra’s lupu is a different word for the same animal. The Hebrew noun and the Midianite’s name have identical spelling, so their index counts overlap. John 10:12 uses the animal word; the proposed automated link to Judg 7:25 is only a match to the proper name. The Peshitta noun is SEDRA lexeme 636."
